## Addendum 2 (2026-11-26, written before any stage-B result on the Open LLM Leaderboard matrix is computed; stage A of that matrix has run and printed only the chosen ranks)
Transfer matrix: Open LLM Leaderboard v2 per-subtask results (`code/transfer/olb_extract.py`, `olb_matrix.py`): 4,507 models x 39 sub-benchmarks, dense (every retained model has all 39), score = the leaderboard's per-subtask normalised
score x 100; one (latest full) result file per model. Types for stratification: bbh (24), math (7), gpqa (3), musr (3), ifeval (1), mmlu_pro (1); C/T splits: 50 splits, |T| = 12, m_T = max(3, ceil(12/3)) = 4 (always met: dense), eligibility
>= k in C; k grid {1,2,3,5,8,13}; rank grid {1,2,3,4,6,8,12,16}. Same rules, scores, splits code, bootstrap (B = 5000, resampling unit = group) as MTEB.
* **Groups (family heuristic) and its limits.** 'Family stem' = first keyword of a fixed list (Qwen, Llama, Mistral, Gemma, Phi, ... in `olb_matrix.py`) found in the model name, else the uploader. 475 groups; the largest ('qwen2.5') has 408 models (9%). Limits: merges and fine-tunes
  keep the stem of the base but a model can match a wrong stem by substring; many uploaders' fine-tunes of one base share training data, so a held-out group can still leak through unlisted derivatives; the date is the evaluation timestamp, not the release date,
  so there is no temporal split on this matrix; models are mostly small open models evaluated under one harness. As labelled sensitivity (if budget allows): grouping by uploader instead.
* **Margins.** The gap-based delta of section F is attainable or not on this matrix; as the sub-benchmark scale is [0,100] and models are dense, the margin used for verdicts is fixed from the floor: **primary here: delta_floor = 0.25 x floor_j** (aggregated over T as for MTEB),
  with the gap-based delta reported next to it. k*(epsilon): epsilon in {delta_floor, 2 delta_floor, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5 of the mean floor (fractions) and 0.5, 1, 2, 3 raw points}; excess over the model's own floor on T; verdict rule unchanged.
* **Claims it is confirmatory for (stated now):** (i) excess over the floor is non-increasing in k up to noise and S6 <= S0 on it for small k; (ii) the same ordering of rules; (iii) the training-side rule of Deviation 4(a) predicts the empirical k*(epsilon) within one grid step at
  epsilon in {delta_floor, 2 delta_floor} in G and S; (iv) the floor misfit (measured floor MSE over the factor model's own noise term) is reported with the same diagnostics as MTEB. Pass/fail of (iii) is reported as such.
* Splits: G (10 folds over 475 groups) and S (strength split, 25% strongest as test), as defined for MTEB; no T.
